From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nl80211: End the wait for a reply on a positive error

send_and_recv_glb() reads replies while err.err is positive, and
error_handler() copies the error of an NLMSG_ERROR message to err.err
unchanged. A kernel answer with a positive error value therefore counts
as no answer: the acknowledgement of the request was read, no other
message follows, and nl_recvmsgs() blocks in recvmsg() for ever. The
event loop stops, and with it every control and ubus interface.

On mt7996 the station request (NL80211_CMD_NEW_STATION or SET_STATION)
of add_associated_sta() was answered with error 65539, apparently a
firmware status that the driver returned as a positive value. hostapd then stopped in the middle of an association.

The value is invalid, but the answer to the request has arrived, so the
wait must end. Take a positive error as -EPROTO and log the raw value
with the message type and command, so that the request fails and the
driver defect stays visible.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
+++ b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
@@ -384,6 +384,15 @@ static int error_handler(struct sockaddr
 	int rem;
 
 	err_args->err = err->error;
+	if (err_args->err > 0) {
+		/* send_and_recv_glb() waits for a reply while err is positive */
+		wpa_printf(MSG_ERROR,
+			   "nl80211: kernel answered message type %u command %u with invalid error %d",
+			   orig_nlh->nlmsg_type,
+			   ((struct genlmsghdr *) nlmsg_data(orig_nlh))->cmd,
+			   err->error);
+		err_args->err = -EPROTO;
+	}
 	if (err_args->err_info)
 		err_args->err_info->link_id = -1;
 
